# ANALYSIS  (evidence, not a gate assertion -- no wall-clock number is
# asserted anywhere in the suite)
#
# slope, ms per record of history (least squares over all 800 samples):
#   BEFORE (15e6ef7)  0.605476  0.587496     range 0.587 - 0.605
#   AFTER  (this tip) 0.035946  0.034872     range 0.035 - 0.036
#   -> RANGES DO NOT OVERLAP. ~17x reduction. The slope is near-flat.
#
# mean latency of the last 50 admissions (history ~750-800), ms:
#   BEFORE   552.67   539.81                 range 540 - 553
#   AFTER    102.04   101.80                 range 102 - 102
#   -> RANGES DO NOT OVERLAP. ~5.3x reduction in steady-state cost.
#
# The SPREAD is itself a finding. AFTER's two reps differ by 0.2% in
# steady-state latency and 3% in slope; BEFORE differs by 2.4% and 3%.
# Both arms ran interleaved on a box carrying another seat's builds
# (loadavg 25-41 throughout), and the AFTER arm's near-immunity to that
# is what a commit that no longer touches the store looks like.
#
# WHAT THIS SHOWS. Section 3d removed the quadratic; section 3c removes
# the linearity of the DURABLE work. The residual 0.035 ms/record is not
# store I/O -- the committed admission reads ZERO durable rows, pinned
# by tests_p0_60_admission_cost::one_admission_does_not_reread_the_
# conversation. It is in-memory: the retained-charge and outbox
# structures the live owner carries, and the observer-progress witness
# vector the reconcile planner walks per commit. Section 5 of the design
# doc names `committed_admissions` as the next ceiling and it is now the
# visible one.
#
# EXTRAPOLATION, on this box and this probe only. A single admission
# crosses a 5s socket window at
#   BEFORE  N ~ (5000 - 148) / 0.587  ~=  8,300 records
#   AFTER   N ~ (5000 -  67) / 0.035  ~= 141,000 records
# The field figure that opened board #60 (1.153 ms/record, fatal at
# N~4,328) was measured over TCP with 9,728-byte payloads at 8c8adec and
# is NOT comparable to either arm here; only BEFORE-vs-AFTER within this
# file is a controlled comparison.
#
# Probe source: crates/liminal-server/src/server/participant/production/
# p0_64_probe.rs, a throwaway #[test] added identically to both trees,
# never committed, removed after the run. Release profile both arms.
